    "title": "Houston Police Officer Killed in Motorcycle Crash While Escorting Traffic - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Daryl Matthews ,\n1 days ago\nHOUSTON (KIAH) – The Houston Police Department is mourning the loss of one of its own after a violent crash on Tuesday.\nOn Wednesday, HPD announced Senior Police Officer Alex Roberts was struck and killed around 4:20 p.m. while conducting a traffic escort on his motorcycle. The department did not give details about what led to the crash; however, Investigators with the Anderson County Sheriff’s Office and the Texas Department of Public Safety are piecing together the deadly collision.\nRoberts worked on the Traffic Enforcement Division’s Solo Motorcycle Detail for 15 years after being sworn in as an officer in November 2010.\nHPD Police Chief J. Noe Diaz, Jr. confirmed the officer’s death, calling it a crushing loss.\n“Senior Police Officer Roberts faithfully served the Houston Police Department with honor and dedication. His loss is felt deeply within our department and the community he proudly served,” said Diaz.\nThe department has asked the community to keep Roberts’ family and his extended HPD family in their thoughts during this time of mourning.\nRoberts’ funeral arrangements have yet to be announced.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to CW39 Houston.",
